---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Chronometric Architecture" description="The A-B-C-D nested timeline layers and where dark matter resides.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>Nested Chronometric Architecture</h1>
    <p class="lead">The early universe was governed by overlapping layers of time. Crucially, these layers did not end—they continue to exist right now, forming a nested structure that defines the behavior of dark matter and cosmic expansion.</p>

    <figure style="margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
      <div style="background: #f1f5f9; height: 300px; border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: #64748b; border: 2px dashed #cbd5e1;">
      <img
        src="/images/Nested_Chronometric_Architecture_Diagram.png"
        alt="Hydrodynamic Particle Map: Dual-dial topology showing intersection depth (mass) and tilt (charge)" 
        style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" 
        loading="lazy"
       />
      </div>
      <figcaption style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic;">Fig 1. The Void (Phase B) encapsulates Threshold Time (Phase C), which encapsulates Local Time (Phase D).</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>The Four Phases</h2>
    <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #334155;">
      <li><strong>Phase A (The Spark):</strong> The timeline first punctures the TSC. This is an event, not a duration.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase B (The Void):</strong> The initial shockwave creates pure Expansion Time. The Void is not just an initial phase; it is the enclosing spatial environment for everything that follows.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase C (The Fringe):</strong> The slow frame-rate layer forms inside the Void. This is the domain of Dark Matter.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase D (The Ignition):</strong> Density crosses the critical threshold inside the Threshold Time layer, and Local Time begins (The CMB).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Overlap: Where Dark Matter Lives</h2>
    <p>Threshold Time does not end when Local Time begins. When Local Time ignited in dense pockets, not all particles crossed the threshold. The particles in the sparse outskirts remained locked in the shallow-coupled state of the Threshold Time layer.</p>
    <p>This overlapping Threshold Time layer is <strong>Dark Matter</strong>. It possesses mass but exhibits zero electric charge because it remains geometrically locked at a 45-degree symmetry.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>